e near 11%, flat on 2026.\n   - **Overall:** Stable and well covered by backlog.\n\n2. **Tarnwell Electric (TRNW)**\n   - **Revenue:** Expected to grow about 6%, driven by price increases.\n   - **Margins:** Operating margin should rise to 14% from 12% in 2026, again on pricing.\n   - **Overall:** The strongest margin story of the five.\n\n3. **Braxen Cable (BRXC)**\n   - **Revenue:** Expected to grow about 2%. Volumes are flat, and the growth comes from pass-through pricing.\n   - **Margins:** Weak. Copper costs are up 18%, and 2027 earnings are expected to be flat.\n   - **Overall:** Modest on revenue and weak on margins.\n\n4. **Ostrand Meters (OSTM)**\n   - **Revenue:** Strong. The Norvane Utilities smart-meter contract adds about 20% to 2027 revenue.\n   - **Margins:** Slightly weaker. Margins dip one point in 2027 as the Norvane rollout ramps.\n   - **Overall:** Strong on revenue, with a small margin cost. Neither source gives a base revenue figure or a margin level.\n\n5. **Kelby Switchgear (KLBS)**\n   - **Revenue:** Expected to fall 5%, as it loses medium-voltage switchgear share to Tarnwell.\n   - **Margins:** Stable. Restructuring holds operating margin at 8%.\n   - **Overall:** The weakest of the five on revenue. The sources give no base revenue figure.\n\nTarnwell's gains and Kelby's losses are connected, since Kelby is losing share to Tarnwell.","ttft_ms":2309,"type":"result","duration_ms":23135,"uuid":"16909eb2-0af3-4f8d-af96-520fd5633ed7","ttft_stream_ms":1555,"time_to_request_ms":258,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":27,"system_prompt":23,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":51,"input_hooks":6,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":11,"tool_pool_refresh":2,"init_message":14,"init_frame_send":13,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":16,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":6,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":25,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":17,"message_normalization":9,"client_creation":11,"request_